e\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A common sickness caused by a virus\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" The flu\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A serious sickness caused by a virus\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Toothache\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A pain in your tooth\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Backache\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A pain in your back\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Cramp\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A sharp pain in a muscle \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Should vs. Must to Talk About Solutions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the modal <span class=\"italic\">should</span> to give advice.<br>   <span class=\"italic\"><br>Example: You should get some rest.<br></span>  <br>You use the modal <span class=\"italic\">must</span> to tell someone what they have to do or need to do. It is very strong.<br>  <span class=\"italic\"><br>Example: You must take medicine.<br></span>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You should get some rest.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You must eat every day.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You should drink this tea.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You must take this medicine.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "cramp", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a sharp and sudden pain in your body", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have bad stomach cramps.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le11ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about remedies.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "remedy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a medicine or treatment for a sickness", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My Aunt Nelly knows some remedies.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le11ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "peppermint", "type": "name"}, {"content": "leaves from a plant of the mint family", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You should try some peppermint tea.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le11ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ginger ale", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a kind of soda made with ginger", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You should try some ginger ale.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le11ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "antacid", "type": "name"}, {"content": "medicine to help stomach acidity", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You should take an antacid.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le11ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to google", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to search for something on the internet using Google", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I googled stomachache remedies.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le11ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "apple cider vinegar", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a type of vinegar made from apples", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I should take apple cider vinegar.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le11ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "flushed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "red and hot skin", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You look flushed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le11ob10aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn4le11ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With your partner, make a list of common health problems you know.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Make a list of possible remedies for each.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compare your list with another group. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss it with your group. Are they the same remedies? What is different?", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about health problems.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about remedies to health issues.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give suggestions about health issues.", "type": "text"}]}]}